# Local environment
.DS_Store
.swp
.swo
*~
*.swp
*.bak

# IDE
.vscode/*
# settings.json contains a real API key and is managed by chezmoi+age
# (see SECRETS.md) — it must never be committed as plaintext again.
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
.idea/

# custom_providers: dtx_providers.env (chezmoi+age, see docs/SECRETS.md) plus
# everything else here is generated locally (litellm-config.yaml embeds a real
# upstream API key server-side, proxy.env is a locally-generated token) — never
# commit any of it. Defense-in-depth: this should never exist inside the repo
# at all (it's a $HOME-level chezmoi destination, see docs/SECRETS.md), but a
# misconfigured local chezmoi.toml has produced exactly that before (2026-09-21
# — see docs/SECRETS.md's "Porque .chezmoi-source/ e não home/" section).
.custom_providers/*
*.sublime-*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Logs and runtime
*.log
.env
.env.local
*.pid

# OS
Thumbs.db
node_modules/

# Temporary
temp/
tmp/
*.tmp
.cache/

# Agent-specific (don't track user sessions/logs)
.claude/sessions/
.claude/logs/
.claude/cache/
# Per Claude Code's own docs: worktrees created by the `EnterWorktree`
# tool/`--worktree` flag land here — never commit them (2026-09-18: an
# orphan gitlink for one of these, `curious-finding-unicorn`, got
# committed with no .gitmodules, breaking `git submodule status` and
# leaving a ghost empty dir on fresh clones — see git history).
.claude/worktrees/
# Defense-in-depth: ~/.claude/ is only ever file-symlinked (CLAUDE.md), never
# whole-directory (see setup.sh), so none of this should ever land under
# dotfiles/.claude/ — these entries just make sure a future mistake can't
# commit live runtime state, credentials included.
.claude/.credentials.json
.claude/history.jsonl
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/daemon.log
.claude/daemon.lock
.claude/daemon.status.json
.claude/.last-cleanup
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.claude/session-env/
.claude/file-history/
.claude/jobs/
.claude/backups/
.claude/projects/
.agents/cache/
.cline/sessions/

# Same defense-in-depth for the other harnesses whose global dirs mix
# versioned config with live runtime state — only their one instructions
# file is ever file-symlinked (see setup.sh), never the directory.
.gemini/history/
.gemini/tmp/
.gemini/state.json
.gemini/trustedFolders.json
.gemini/installation_id
.gemini/projects.json
.codex/*.sqlite
.codex/*.sqlite-shm
.codex/*.sqlite-wal
.codex/installation_id
.codex/herdr-agent-state.sh
.codex/tmp/
.codex/.tmp/
.copilot/session-store.db
.copilot/session-store.db-shm
.copilot/session-store.db-wal
.copilot/logs/
.copilot/config.json
.copilot/command-history-state.json
.copilot/open-sessions-state.json
.copilot/session-state/
.copilot/sidebar-sessions-state/
.copilot/servers/
.copilot/installed-plugins/
.copilot/installed-plugins.lock
.copilot/ide/
.copilot/sessions/

# tasks/lifecycle.py's CAS Layer A sidecar lock (tasks/plans/
# human-in-the-loop-notifications.md §2) — a local, machine-specific lock
# file, never a fact about task state. events.jsonl is the source of
# truth; this is purely a flock() target, never read back for meaning.
tasks/.events.lock

# tasks/sweep.py's heartbeat (§4) — an mtime-only liveness marker for
# tasks/brief.py to check, not a fact worth versioning.
tasks/.sweep-heartbeat

# tasks/claims.py's claim log + sidecar lock (tasks/plans/claim-protocol.md
# §C) — live, machine-local, TTL-bounded coordination state, deliberately
# NOT durable: losing it just means everyone re-claims. The permanent
# audit trail stays in tasks/events.jsonl via --team/--handoff.
tasks/claims.jsonl
tasks/.claims.lock

# tasks/dispatch.py's log for providers with no confirmed background-
# launch flag (copilot/agy — only Claude Code's --bg is confirmed) —
# stdout/stderr from a detached process, not a fact about task state.
tasks/.dispatch-logs/

# But DO track core configs
!.claude/
!.agents/
!.vscode/
!.github/
!.gemini/
!.codex/
!.copilot/

# tasks/worktree.py's per-machine worktree view (one <task-id>.md per card
# with a managed worktree + README.md index). Machine-local paths — never
# committed, so the tracked cards next to it never churn.
tasks/cards/worktrees/
